## AD-032

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-032
**TITLE:** Every First-Class Object Owns Only Its Own Lifecycle — No Lifecycle May Extend Backwards Into the Lifecycle of Another First-Class Object
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** COMMITMENT_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-E

### Decision Statement

Every first-class object within Black Umbrella owns only its own lifecycle. No lifecycle may extend backwards into the lifecycle of another first-class object. Each object begins at its own creation event and owns no states belonging to another object.

### Context

This principle was identified during Stage 2 review when a draft Commitment lifecycle included a state ("Proposed") that preceded the Commitment's creation event and therefore belonged to the Proposal's lifecycle. The review identified this as a violation of lifecycle ownership. Rather than recording the correction only in the context of Commitments, it was recognised as a general architectural rule applicable to all first-class objects in the Black Umbrella operating model.

### Rationale

Lifecycle boundary violations produce ambiguity about which object owns a state, which standard governs a transition, and which system is responsible for tracking it. Enforcing clean lifecycle ownership boundaries means that every state has exactly one owner, every transition has exactly one governing standard, and every object's lifecycle is self-contained and legible without reference to another object's lifecycle. This property is required for AIOS to orchestrate cleanly.

### Impact

All current and future Black Umbrella Operating Standards shall define object lifecycles that begin at the object's creation event. No state may be added to an object's lifecycle that predates that object's existence. Where a handoff between objects occurs (e.g. Proposal → Commitment), the boundary is recorded through references, not through shared or overlapping lifecycle states. This rule shall be applied when defining the lifecycles of Operating Areas, Offices, and all future first-class objects.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** COMMITMENT_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
- **Queue Status:** Awaiting Execute
- **Supersedes:** None
- **Superseded By:** None

### References

- Black Umbrella Commitment Standard
- COMMITMENT_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- AD-031 (Commitment lifecycle begins at Instantiated)

