## AD-033

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-033
**TITLE:** Operating Areas Are Instantiated Execution Context Instances Derived From Operating Area Templates
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** COMMITMENT_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-F

### Decision Statement

Operating Areas are execution contexts. Each Operating Area is an instance derived from an Operating Area Template. Templates belong to Black Umbrella and define the execution context type. Instances belong exclusively to the Commitment that instantiated them. When a Commitment closes, every instantiated Operating Area belonging to that Commitment closes with it.

### Context

The Stage 1 architectural discussion established that Operating Areas are not permanent organisational structures. They are execution context types that Commitments instantiate when they are created. This distinction — template vs instance — is fundamental to the commitment-centric architecture. Without it, Operating Areas would be treated as standing organisational units owned by Offices, reverting to the organisation-centric model the Commitment Standard supersedes.

### Rationale

Treating Operating Areas as templates that Commitments instantiate achieves three things. First, it keeps the Operating Area definition stable and reusable across multiple Commitments without creating organisational permanence. Second, it gives each Commitment its own scoped execution contexts with specific inputs, outputs, and completion criteria. Third, it ensures that when a Commitment closes, its execution contexts close cleanly without orphaning permanent organisational structures. This mirrors sound software design principles (object instantiation) while remaining human-legible.

### Impact

The Operating Area Standard shall define a catalogue of Operating Area Templates. Each template defines purpose, required inputs, expected outputs, completion criteria, and execution lifecycle. When a Commitment is instantiated, AIOS creates Operating Area instances from the templates specified in the originating Proposal. The Operating Area execution lifecycle is deferred to the Operating Area Standard.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** COMMITMENT_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
- **Queue Status:** Awaiting Execute
- **Supersedes:** None
- **Superseded By:** None

