## AD-034

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-034
**TITLE:** Commitments Own Operating Areas — Operating Areas Own Execution Contexts — Offices Own Capability
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** COMMITMENT_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-G

### Decision Statement

Commitments own work. Operating Areas own execution contexts. Offices own capability. These are three distinct and non-overlapping ownership responsibilities. Offices never own Commitments. Offices never own Operating Areas. Offices fulfil Operating Areas assigned by AIOS. Office accountability is measured by fulfilment quality rather than ownership of work.

### Context

The Stage 1 architectural discussion identified two possible organisational models for Black Umbrella: organisation-centric (Offices own work and Operating Areas) and commitment-centric (Commitments own work, Operating Areas own execution contexts, Offices own capability). The discussion concluded that the commitment-centric model is architecturally correct because it allows AIOS to route work to capable Offices dynamically, prevents work ownership from being tied to which Office currently exists, and gives the Commitment stable operational identity regardless of which agents or Offices fulfil it.

### Rationale

Clear ownership separation removes ambiguity from every operational interaction. When an Office changes its agents, the Commitment is unaffected. When a Commitment closes, the Operating Area closes, but the Office retains its capability. When AIOS routes an Operating Area to a different Office, the Commitment's ownership is unchanged. Each layer has one responsibility and is accountable for exactly that responsibility — nothing more.

### Impact

All Operating Standards, Office definitions, and AIOS orchestration logic shall treat ownership as defined by this decision. Offices are capability providers. They are never listed as owners of Commitments or Operating Areas in any standard, register, or system. Fulfilment responsibility is assigned by AIOS at runtime; it is not permanent ownership. Future standards defining Offices shall describe capability ownership, not work ownership.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** COMMITMENT_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
- **Queue Status:** Awaiting Execute
- **Supersedes:** None
- **Superseded By:** None

