## AD-038

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-038
**TITLE:** Operating Area Templates and Operating Area Instances Are Distinct Architectural Objects
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OPERATING_AREA_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-B

### Decision Statement

Operating Area Templates and Operating Area Instances are distinct architectural objects with different ownership, scope, and lifecycle. Templates are permanent governance definitions belonging to Black Umbrella. Instances are transient execution contexts belonging exclusively to the Commitment that instantiated them.

### Context

Without this distinction, Operating Areas could be confused with permanent organisational units. The template/instance model mirrors the architectural principle established in the Commitment Standard: "Operating Area Templates belong to Black Umbrella. Instances belong to individual Commitments." This decision records that distinction as a permanent governance rule.

### Rationale

The Template/Instance separation achieves several properties simultaneously. Templates remain stable and reusable across multiple Commitments without creating organisational permanence. Instances are scoped to their Commitment and close when it closes. The Operating Area Standard can evolve the template catalogue through governance without affecting live instances. This separation is fundamental to AIOS orchestration: AIOS instantiates from templates and orchestrates instances.

### Impact

The Operating Area Standard shall maintain a governed template catalogue. Every template is permanent until superseded through governance. Every instance is transient and belongs to exactly one Commitment. No system or agent may create Operating Area Instances outside of the Commitment instantiation process.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** OPERATING_AREA_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
