## AD-041

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-041
**TITLE:** Operating Area Templates Are Derived Using Three Orchestration Tests — Distinct Capability, Independent Completion, Independent Blockage
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OPERATING_AREA_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-E

### Decision Statement

An execution context becomes its own Operating Area Template when one or more of three orchestration tests is satisfied: (1) the execution requires independently routable capability; (2) the execution possesses its own meaningful completion event; (3) the execution may become blocked independently of neighbouring execution contexts. If none of these tests are satisfied, the work remains an internal execution activity within an existing Operating Area.

### Context

The Stage 1 architectural discussion established that the Operating Area Template catalogue must be derived from orchestration requirements rather than invented through organisational intuition. The question "what determines when something deserves to become its own Operating Area?" was resolved through the principle: "the test is whether AIOS needs to route it, track its state, or complete it independently." The three tests formalise this principle.

### Rationale

Deriving templates from orchestration requirements rather than organisational categories ensures the catalogue remains grounded in operational necessity. It prevents the catalogue from growing through intuition, habit, or copying external frameworks. It also provides a stable, objective criterion for evaluating proposed new templates: any submission to the governed amendment process must demonstrate that at least one of the three tests is satisfied.

### Impact

The Operating Area Template Catalogue shall be extended only by templates that satisfy at least one of the three derivation tests. Governance review of proposed templates shall apply these tests explicitly. Templates derived from organisational preference, familiarity, or analogy to external frameworks, without satisfying at least one test, shall be rejected.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** OPERATING_AREA_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
- **Queue Status:** Awaiting Execute
- **Supersedes:** None
- **Superseded By:** None

