## AD-042

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-042
**TITLE:** Every Operating Area Shall Execute Under a Mandatory Execution Contract Containing the Required Contract Components Defined by This Standard
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OPERATING_AREA_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-F

### Decision Statement

Every Operating Area Template shall define: Operational Purpose, Required Inputs, Expected Deliverable, Deliverable Form, Verification Criteria, Completion Criteria, Execution Lifecycle, and Required Capability. Required Capability is the capability specification AIOS consumes when matching the Operating Area to an appropriate Office — templates declare capability requirements, never Office assignments. Templates missing any mandatory component fail this standard.

### Context

Without mandatory contract components, template quality becomes variable and AIOS consumption becomes unreliable. The execution contract is the mechanism through which AIOS can determine state, responsibility, and completion without inference. If any contract component is absent, AIOS cannot satisfy the Consumption Test for that Operating Area.

### Rationale

Mandatory components ensure every template is complete before it enters the catalogue. The distinction between Required Capability (a specification) and Office Assignment (a binding) is explicitly captured here to prevent future templates from coupling execution context to organisational structure. Templates that name specific Offices violate the commitment-centric architecture by pre-determining the Office capability model.

### Impact

The governed amendment process for new template entries shall verify all eight mandatory contract components are present and correctly specified before the template is accepted into the catalogue. Existing templates missing any component shall be flagged as incomplete and updated through governance before use.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** OPERATING_AREA_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
