## AD-044

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-044
**TITLE:** Version 1 Dependency Graphs Support Sequential Completion Gates Only
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OPERATING_AREA_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-H

### Decision Statement

Version 1 Dependency Graphs support sequential completion gates only. A downstream Operating Area may activate only after all prerequisite Operating Areas have produced verified Deliverables. Partial completion gates, event triggers, milestone activations, and intermediate contracts are not supported in Version 1.

### Context

The Stage 1 discussion identified that partial dependencies — where a downstream Operating Area can activate based on an intermediate output of an upstream Operating Area — would require Operating Areas to define intermediate completion states, significantly increasing contract complexity and AIOS inference requirements. Starting with completion gates keeps contracts simple, AIOS deterministic, templates understandable, and review straightforward.

### Rationale

Introducing complexity only when governance requires it is a consistent Black Umbrella design principle. Completion gates cover the majority of dependency scenarios without requiring Operating Areas to expose internal state. Future amendments can introduce more sophisticated dependency models when operational evidence demonstrates their necessity.

### Impact

All Version 1 Dependency Graphs shall use completion gates exclusively. AIOS routing logic in Version 1 shall only evaluate verified Deliverable existence as an activation condition. Advanced dependency semantics are explicitly deferred and shall be introduced only through a governed amendment to this decision.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** OPERATING_AREA_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
