## AD-047

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-047
**TITLE:** An Operating Area Template Is Complete Only When It Satisfies the AIOS Consumption Test
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OPERATING_AREA_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-K

### Decision Statement

An Operating Area Template is complete only if AIOS can determine directly, without inference: current execution state, required capability, Deliverable existence, Deliverable verification, and completion. If AIOS cannot determine any of these directly from the template contract, the template is incomplete.

### Context

The AIOS Consumption Test emerged from the Stage 1 discussion and was refined during review: "Can AIOS determine state, responsibility and completion directly from the standard without inference?" A template that requires AIOS to infer any of the five items is underspecified. This test provides an objective, machine-evaluable completeness criterion for templates — replacing reviewer judgement with a deterministic check.

### Rationale

An objective completeness test prevents the template catalogue from accumulating underspecified entries. It also ensures that AIOS remains an orchestration layer rather than an interpretation layer: every template either passes the test (AIOS can consume it directly) or fails (governance must improve it before it enters the catalogue). There is no middle ground. This is consistent with the broader principle that ambiguity belongs to governance, not to runtime execution.

### Impact

Every proposed template shall be assessed against the AIOS Consumption Test before entering the catalogue. The five test criteria are mandatory. Governance review of template proposals shall explicitly evaluate each criterion. Templates that pass all five criteria are eligible for the catalogue; those that fail any criterion must be revised through governance before acceptance.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** OPERATING_AREA_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
- **Queue Status:** Awaiting Execute
- **Supersedes:** None
- **Superseded By:** None

### References

- Black Umbrella Operating Area Standard
- OPERATING_AREA_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- AD-035 (AIOS orchestrates Commitments)
- AD-042 (Mandatory execution contract)

