## AD-048

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-048
**TITLE:** The Operating Area Template Catalogue Shall Evolve Only Through Governed Amendment to This Standard
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OPERATING_AREA_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-L

### Decision Statement

The Operating Area Template Catalogue shall evolve only through governed amendment to the Operating Area Standard. New templates shall be introduced only through this governed process. The catalogue is intentionally open — it is not a closed enumeration — but every addition requires governance approval.

### Context

An uncontrolled template catalogue would accumulate entries based on convenience, habit, or analogy rather than architectural necessity. The three derivation tests (AD-041) provide the objective criterion for new templates. Requiring governed amendment to add templates ensures every entry has been evaluated against those tests and approved by the Founder.

### Rationale

Governed catalogue evolution preserves architectural integrity over time. It prevents the catalogue from becoming an ad-hoc collection of informally recognised work types. It also ensures that future AIOS implementations remain aligned with the governed template set — AIOS cannot be required to orchestrate a template that doesn't exist in the approved catalogue.

### Impact

No new Operating Area Template may be added to the catalogue without a governed amendment. The amendment Proposal must demonstrate that the proposed template satisfies at least one of the three derivation tests. Existing templates may be refined through the same process. Template retirement requires a governed amendment noting the retirement reason and any affected Commitments.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** OPERATING_AREA_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
