## AD-050

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-050
**TITLE:** Every Office Owns Exactly One Registered Capability
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-B

### Decision Statement

Every Office owns exactly one Registered Capability. Multiple Capabilities shall never exist within one Office. Capabilities are distinct whenever AIOS would make a different routing decision.

### Context

Capability atomicity is required for deterministic routing. If an Office declared multiple capabilities, AIOS would need to interpret which capability applies to a given Operating Area. That interpretation introduces ambiguity incompatible with the deterministic routing model.

### Rationale

One Office per registered capability ensures AIOS can route deterministically from an Operating Area's Required Capability declaration to exactly one Office. The routing test — whether AIOS would make a different routing decision — is the single sufficient criterion for capability distinctness. Secondary characteristics such as quality standard declarations or fulfilment models do not determine capability identity.

### Impact

Where a distinction in routing behaviour exists, governance shall establish a separate Office. An existing Office shall never expand its scope to accommodate a second capability. Capability separation must be resolved through a new Office registration, not through amendment to an existing Office.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
- **Queue Status:** Awaiting Execute
- **Supersedes:** None
- **Superseded By:** None

