## AD-051

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-051
**TITLE:** Capabilities Are Persistent Organisational Objects Independent of Fulfilment Technology
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-C

### Decision Statement

Capabilities are persistent governance objects. They persist independently of individual people, AI systems, software platforms, and implementation technologies.

### Context

Previous organisational models often bound capability to specific individuals, tools, or technologies. This creates fragility: when the person leaves or the technology changes, the capability record is disrupted. Black Umbrella requires an organisational architecture stable across technology generations.

### Rationale

Treating capability as a persistent governance object — separate from any specific fulfilment mechanism — ensures the organisational capability record remains stable regardless of how that capability is currently fulfilled. The Office owns the capability permanently. How it is fulfilled at any given moment is an implementation detail outside the governance record.

### Impact

Capability records in the Office Registry shall never reference specific executors, AI systems, individuals, or software platforms. The registered capability is the persistent governance object. Fulfilment mechanisms may change freely without requiring a governance event, provided the registered capability and Quality Standard Declaration remain unchanged.

### Governance Status

