## AD-052

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-052
**TITLE:** Capability Declarations Shall Use the Controlled Black Umbrella Capability Vocabulary
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-D

### Decision Statement

All capability declarations shall use the approved Black Umbrella Capability Vocabulary. No synonym, alias, or inferred equivalence is permitted. Version 1 establishes: Research, Strategy, Commercial, Documentation, Client Management, Coordination, Delivery, Quality Review.

### Context

Deterministic routing requires that AIOS can match an Operating Area's Required Capability declaration to an Office's Registered Capability declaration without semantic interpretation. If different vocabulary were used across standards, AIOS would require a translation layer, introducing ambiguity and potential routing errors.

### Rationale

A shared controlled vocabulary consumed by both the Operating Area Standard and the Office Standard ensures that AIOS performs direct string matching rather than semantic reasoning. The vocabulary becomes the routing contract between Operating Areas and Offices. Governing its evolution through amendment prevents vocabulary drift.

### Impact

Operating Area Templates shall declare Required Capability using only the approved vocabulary. Office registrations shall declare Registered Capability using only the approved vocabulary. AIOS performs deterministic matching using this shared vocabulary. Any new capability term must be introduced through a governed amendment before it may appear in any Operating Area Template or Office registration.

### Governance Status

