## AD-053

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-053
**TITLE:** The Office Registry Is the Authoritative Source of Organisational Capability
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-E

### Decision Statement

Every Office shall be permanently recorded within the Office Registry. The Office Registry is the authoritative source of organisational capability and is consumed by AIOS for deterministic routing. It is never modified during runtime execution.

### Context

For AIOS to perform deterministic routing, it must have access to a single, authoritative record of all registered capabilities and their owning Offices. Without a permanent registry, capability records would be distributed, inconsistent, or subject to runtime modification.

### Rationale

The Office Registry serves the same architectural role for capability that the Architecture Decision Register serves for governance — it is the permanent, authoritative, and immutable-during-execution record. Prohibiting runtime modification ensures AIOS routing is always based on governed capability declarations, never on transient operational state.

### Impact

The Office Registry shall be established and maintained as a governed document. Its contents shall reflect only capabilities approved through the WLS. AIOS shall consume the Office Registry as a read-only input during routing. No operational event may modify the Office Registry without a preceding governance event.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
