## AD-054

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-054
**TITLE:** Offices Are Created Only Through Governance and Administrative Registration
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-F

### Decision Statement

An Office comes into existence only through governance. Founder Approval authorises creation. Administrative registration creates the Office Registry entry. An Office shall never be created by a Commitment, an Operating Area, AIOS, runtime execution, or implementation activity.

### Context

The Lifecycle Ownership Rule (AD-032) establishes that every first-class object owns only its own lifecycle. The Office lifecycle must therefore begin through a governance event, not through operational activity. Without this rule, Commitments or AIOS could implicitly create capability registrations, undermining the authoritative nature of the Office Registry.

### Rationale

Restricting Office creation to governance ensures every registered capability has been explicitly approved by the Founder. This prevents capability from accumulating informally through operational necessity. It also ensures that AIOS routing is always based on deliberately governed capability records rather than emergent operational artifacts.

### Impact

Any requirement for a new capability must be addressed through a Proposal before the capability can be registered. A Proposal that requires a capability not yet in the Office Registry is incomplete and cannot proceed until the required Office is established through a separate governance process.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
