## AD-055

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-055
**TITLE:** Internal Capability Improvement Belongs to the Office Without Governance Event
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-G

### Decision Statement

Every Office owns the continuous improvement of its Registered Capability. Internal improvements to processes, methods, tooling, agents, and execution practices require no governance event provided the Office Registration remains unchanged.

### Context

Effective organisations must be able to improve how they fulfil their responsibilities without administrative overhead. Requiring governance approval for every internal improvement would create friction incompatible with continuous improvement. At the same time, changes that affect the governance record must remain governed.

### Rationale

The separation between internal improvement (Office-owned, no governance) and registered capability changes (requires governance) mirrors the principle applied throughout the architecture: governance governs governance objects, not implementation details. Internal improvement is an implementation detail. The registered capability and quality standard are governance objects.

### Impact

Offices may freely change their internal processes, tools, agents, and methods without initiating a governance event, provided these changes do not alter the Registered Capability, Quality Standard Declaration, or routing characteristics. The Office is accountable for maintaining its declared quality standard through whatever internal means it chooses.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
