## AD-057

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-057
**TITLE:** Every Office Shall Maintain One Quality Standard Declaration
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-I

### Decision Statement

Every Office shall register one Quality Standard Declaration. The declaration shall specify the criteria that determine acceptable fulfilment of the Registered Capability. The Deliverable requirements defined by the Operating Area Standard establish the minimum acceptable baseline. Office-specific quality commitments may extend those requirements but shall never weaken them.

### Context

Without a declared quality standard, Stage 5 review has no objective basis for evaluating Office performance. The Office's accountability for Deliverable quality would be unenforceable. A Quality Standard Declaration transforms quality accountability from an aspiration into a verifiable governance commitment.

### Rationale

The Quality Standard Declaration creates an objective, registered quality commitment against which AIOS and Stage 5 can evaluate Deliverables. By requiring that Office-specific criteria extend but never weaken the Operating Area Standard baseline, the architecture ensures a minimum quality floor across all capabilities while permitting Offices to declare higher standards appropriate to their capability.

### Impact

Every Office registration shall include a Quality Standard Declaration. A Proposal creating an Office without a Quality Standard Declaration is incomplete. The AIOS Standard will define the evaluation framework consuming these declarations during Stage 5 review.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
