## AD-061

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-061
**TITLE:** The Initial Office Registry Evolves Only Through Governed Amendment
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-M

### Decision Statement

The Initial Office Registry established by Version 1 of the Office Standard evolves only through governed amendment to the Office Standard. Future Offices may be introduced only through this governed process.

### Context

An uncontrolled registry would accumulate entries based on operational convenience rather than architectural necessity. Requiring governed amendment to add Offices ensures every entry has been evaluated against the capability atomicity rule and approved by the Founder.

### Rationale

Governed registry evolution preserves architectural integrity over time. It prevents the Office Registry from becoming an ad-hoc collection of informally recognised capabilities. It also ensures that future AIOS implementations remain aligned with the governed Office set — AIOS cannot be required to route to an Office that doesn't exist in the approved registry.

### Impact

No new Office may be added to the Office Registry without a governed amendment. The amendment Proposal must demonstrate that the proposed Office owns a distinct, independently routable capability. Existing Offices may be amended through the same process. Office retirement requires a governed event noting the retirement reason and any affected Commitments.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
