## AD-062

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-062
**TITLE:** The Controlled Capability Vocabulary Evolves Only Through Governed Amendment
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-003
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-N

### Decision Statement

The Controlled Capability Vocabulary established by Version 1 of the Office Standard evolves only through governed amendment to the Office Standard. Future capability terms may be introduced only through this governed process.

### Context

The controlled vocabulary is the routing contract between Operating Area Templates and Offices. If the vocabulary could evolve informally, routing ambiguity would accumulate silently. AIOS would encounter capability terms in Operating Area Templates that do not appear in the Office Registry, or vice versa.

### Rationale

Governing vocabulary evolution ensures that every capability term used in an Operating Area Template has a corresponding registered Office, and every registered Office has a matching capability term. This bidirectional integrity is required for deterministic routing. Governed amendment also ensures that new terms are evaluated against the capability atomicity rule before being admitted to the vocabulary.

### Impact

No new capability term may be used in any Operating Area Template or Office registration without first being introduced through a governed amendment to the Office Standard. The amendment Proposal must include both the new vocabulary term and the corresponding Office registration. Terms may not be introduced in isolation.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** OFFICE_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
- **Queue Status:** Awaiting Execute
- **Supersedes:** None
- **Superseded By:** None

