## AD-063

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-063
**TITLE:** AIOS Shall Operate Exclusively Through a Generic Operational Event Engine
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-001
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-A

### Decision Statement

AIOS shall operate exclusively through a generic Operational Event engine. Every AIOS behaviour shall follow one pattern regardless of event source: receive, validate, determine consequences, execute deterministic consequences, record operational history, escalate where Founder judgment is required.

### Context

A generic engine ensures AIOS applies uniform logic to every governance object without privileging any particular event type. If AIOS had bespoke processing paths for specific event types, it would implicitly assign priority to those objects — a judgment AIOS is not authorised to make. The significance of any event type derives from governance, not from AIOS architecture.

### Rationale

A single generic engine ensures AIOS remains neutral across all governance objects. It also ensures the engine remains stable as new event types are introduced through governed amendment. Adding a new event type requires no change to the engine — only a new event source and consequence rule.

### Impact

Every AIOS behaviour must be expressible within the generic event engine pattern. No bespoke processing path may be introduced for any specific event type or governance object. Future AIOS amendments must demonstrate compatibility with the generic engine before approval.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
- **Queue Status:** Awaiting Execute
- **Supersedes:** None
- **Superseded By:** None

### References

- Black Umbrella AIOS Standard
- AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md

