## AD-064

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-064
**TITLE:** Every AIOS Behaviour Shall Originate From an Operational Event
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-001
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-B

### Decision Statement

Every AIOS behaviour shall originate from an Operational Event. No AIOS behaviour may be initiated without a preceding Operational Event.

### Context

Without this constraint, AIOS could initiate behaviour autonomously — acting on internal state, timers, or predictions rather than on governance events. Autonomous initiation would place AIOS outside the governance model and create behaviour that cannot be traced to a governance authority.

### Rationale

Requiring every behaviour to originate from an Operational Event ensures complete traceability. Every AIOS action can be traced to a specific event, which can be traced to a specific governance transition, which can be traced to a specific governance object and authority. This makes AIOS behaviour fully auditable.

### Impact

AIOS shall not initiate behaviour proactively, predictively, or autonomously. All behaviour is reactive. Scheduled or time-triggered behaviour requires a governed mechanism that produces an Operational Event. The event is always the trigger.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
- **Queue Status:** Awaiting Execute
- **Supersedes:** None
- **Superseded By:** None

