## AD-065

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-065
**TITLE:** Operational Events Shall Be Classified as Either Progression Events or Exception Events
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-001
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-C

### Decision Statement

Every Operational Event belongs to exactly one category: Progression Event or Exception Event. Category determines consequence behaviour. Category never alters validation behaviour.

### Context

Two categories of operational reality require different AIOS responses. Progression Events advance the approved governance model. Exception Events interrupt it. Without formal classification, AIOS would need to infer which type of response is appropriate — a judgment AIOS is not authorised to make. Classification through governance removes that inference requirement.

### Rationale

Formal event categorisation ensures AIOS behaviour is deterministic by category. Consequence rules differ between Progression and Exception events. Validation rules are identical. This separation ensures AIOS never interprets whether an event is good or bad — category is declared by governance, not assessed by AIOS.

### Impact

Every Operational Event type defined in this standard or future amendments must be assigned to exactly one category at the time of definition. Unclassified event types are not valid. Category assignment is a governance decision made at the time the event type is defined.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
- **Queue Status:** Awaiting Execute
- **Supersedes:** None
- **Superseded By:** None

