## AD-068

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-068
**TITLE:** Founder Execute Shall Target Commitments
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-001
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-F

### Decision Statement

The Founder Execute instruction shall target the Commitment. The Founder authorises execution at the operational object level. AIOS performs the required governance validation internally.

### Context

The Work Lifecycle Standard Stage 4 entry conditions reference Architecture Decisions. The Commitment Standard introduced the Commitment as the operational object. The Founder must interact with the operational model at the operational level — targeting Commitments — rather than at the governance record level. AIOS bridges this by validating the underlying ADs as part of Commitment activation.

### Rationale

Targeting Commitments keeps the Founder's interaction at the appropriate operational level. The Founder authorises work, not governance records. AIOS translates that authorisation into governance validation. This also future-proofs the Execute model: changes to the underlying AD structure do not require changes to how the Founder issues Execute instructions.

### Impact

Execute instructions not targeting a specific Commitment are invalid. Unqualified Execute instructions are invalid. AIOS shall reject any Execute instruction that does not identify a specific Commitment in a valid Instantiated state.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
