## AD-069

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-069
**TITLE:** AIOS Shall Validate All Stage 4 Entry Conditions Before Authorising Commitment Activation
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-001
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-G

### Decision Statement

Before activating a Commitment, AIOS shall validate all Work Lifecycle Standard Stage 4 entry conditions: Commitment exists, Founder Approval has been granted, required Architecture Decisions are administratively registered, and required Architecture Decisions are present in the Approved Decision Queue.

### Context

The Founder Execute instruction targets the Commitment, but governance requires that the underlying ADs are properly registered before execution may begin. AIOS bridges the operational layer (Commitment) and the governance layer (ADs) by performing this validation automatically. The Founder is not required to verify AD registration status manually.

### Rationale

Automatic Stage 4 validation by AIOS ensures governance prerequisites are always satisfied before execution begins. It also ensures the Founder cannot accidentally activate a Commitment whose underlying governance is incomplete. AIOS becomes the governance enforcement layer at the activation boundary without requiring the Founder to engage with governance records directly.

### Impact

AIOS shall not activate any Commitment without successful Stage 4 validation. A failed validation shall produce a Governance-Required Exception Event and prepare Founder information identifying the unmet entry condition. Partial validation is not permitted — all conditions must be satisfied before activation proceeds.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
