## AD-071

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-071
**TITLE:** AIOS Shall Perform Deterministic Capability Routing Using the Office Registry and Controlled Capability Vocabulary
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-001
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-I

### Decision Statement

AIOS shall route Operating Areas to Offices by reading the Required Capability from the Operating Area Template, reading the Office Registry, and matching using the Controlled Capability Vocabulary. AIOS shall never select capability through inference. AIOS shall never modify capability registrations.

### Context

Deterministic routing requires a shared vocabulary consumed identically by Operating Area Templates and the Office Registry. Without a controlled vocabulary and a single authoritative registry, AIOS would need to resolve routing ambiguities through inference — a judgment it is not authorised to make.

### Rationale

Direct vocabulary matching between Operating Area Required Capability and Office Registered Capability ensures routing is always deterministic, traceable, and governance-derived. The Office Registry is the sole source of routing truth. AIOS consumes it as-registered. Any change to routing behaviour requires a governance change to the Office Registry or the Controlled Capability Vocabulary.

### Impact

AIOS shall reject any routing request where the Required Capability does not appear in the Controlled Capability Vocabulary or does not match a Registered Office in the Office Registry. Such failures shall produce Routing Failure Exception Events. AIOS shall never attempt alternative routing through inference or approximation.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
