## AD-073

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-073
**TITLE:** AIOS Shall Never Perform Strategic Evaluation
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-001
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-K

### Decision Statement

AIOS shall never assess organisational value, strategic success, future direction, or governance quality. Those responsibilities belong exclusively to the Founder. AIOS evaluates only criteria declared through pre-governed objects.

### Context

Strategic evaluation requires contextual judgment about organisational purpose that cannot be pre-declared in governance. If AIOS performed strategic evaluation, it would be making organisational decisions that governance has not authorised. The Founder Judgment Boundary reserves all strategic evaluation for the Founder.

### Rationale

The Pre-Declaration Principle restricts AIOS to evaluating only criteria declared in advance through governance. Strategic evaluation inherently requires criteria that are not pre-declared — they emerge from organisational context and Founder intent. Prohibiting strategic evaluation keeps AIOS entirely within its authorised operational scope.

### Impact

AIOS shall not include any strategic assessment, recommendation, or judgment in the Stage 5 evidence package. AIOS shall not infer whether a Commitment was successful. AIOS shall not suggest future Commitments or governance changes. All such determinations belong to the Founder at Stage 5.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
