## AD-074

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-074
**TITLE:** AIOS Shall Evaluate Only Criteria Declared Through Pre-Governed Objects
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-001
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-L

### Decision Statement

AIOS may evaluate a criterion only if that criterion has been declared through an approved governance object before execution begins. If governance has not pre-declared an objective rule, AIOS shall not evaluate it. That responsibility belongs to the Founder.

### Context

This is the Pre-Declaration Principle — the governing boundary between AIOS determination and Founder judgment. It emerged across all three Stage 1 discussions as the single principle capable of cleanly separating operational evaluation from strategic judgment. The richer and more specific the governance declarations, the more AIOS can determine objectively, and the less strategic overhead falls on the Founder.

### Rationale

Pre-declaration ensures that every AIOS evaluation is traceable to an approved governance record. It prevents AIOS from applying criteria not authorised by governance. It also creates a design incentive: precise governance declarations reduce Founder burden at Stage 5 and expand safe AIOS autonomy. Good governance expands operational autonomy. Poor governance requires more Founder involvement.

### Impact

AIOS implementation shall be able to trace every evaluation it performs to a specific pre-declared governance criterion. Any evaluation that cannot be so traced is outside AIOS authority. Future amendments to AIOS behaviour require the corresponding governance declaration to pre-exist or be introduced simultaneously.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
