## AD-075

**IDENTIFIER:** AD-075
**TITLE:** Operational Outcome Shall Be Objectively Determined by AIOS
**STATUS:** Approved — Awaiting Execute
**REGISTERED:** 2026-07-03
**INITIATIVE:** INI-001
**OWNER:** Black Umbrella Governance
**SOURCE PROPOSAL:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
**TEMPORARY REFERENCE:** AD-M

### Decision Statement

Operational Outcome is determined objectively by AIOS from pre-declared governance. Version 1 defines three values: Successful, Partial, Failed. Operational Outcome represents execution quality only. It shall never consider organisational strategy.

### Context

Commitment closure requires an objective record of execution quality. Without a formally determined Operational Outcome, the historical record would be ambiguous about whether execution succeeded or failed. AIOS is the authoritative source of execution history and is therefore the appropriate body to determine Operational Outcome from pre-declared governance criteria.

### Rationale

An objectively determined Operational Outcome protects Office accountability. Offices whose Deliverables passed every Quality Standard should not face adverse review because the originating Proposal misunderstood the problem. The Operational Outcome accurately records execution reality regardless of strategic outcome. AIOS evaluation of Operational Outcome is final — it is not subject to retrospective appeal at Stage 5.

### Impact

AIOS shall automatically determine Operational Outcome when a Commitment enters Under Review. The determination shall be derived entirely from Deliverable verification history, Quality Standard compliance, and Dependency Graph completion. It shall be included in the Stage 5 evidence package as an objective, non-appealable finding.

### Governance Status

- **Proposal:** AIOS_STANDARD_PROPOSAL_2026-07-03_V1.md
- **Founder Approval:** Granted — 2026-07-03
- **Registered:** 2026-07-03
