## AD-085 — OA Owner Model

**Identifier:** AD-085
**Status:** Approved
**Approved:** 2026-07-05
**Registered:** 2026-07-05
**Initiative:** INI-001

### Decision

Outstanding Actions (OAs) carry an Owner field that decouples ownership from any fixed organisational structure. The Owner field accepts any named entity — an AI Office, an individual (Founder, Human Developer), or an external party — rather than coupling ownership permanently to the Office architecture.

### Valid Owner Values (V1)

- Development Office
- Research Office
- Security Office
- Founder Office
- Founder (personal action)
- Human Developer
- External Contractor
- Unassigned

### Rationale

Locking OA ownership to a fixed set of Offices would require a schema migration each time a new Office is introduced. The Owner field future-proofs the OA model: new owners can be added without changing the data schema. This also allows OAs to be owned by entities that are not Offices (the Founder personally, a contractor, a developer).

### Boundary

This decision governs the OA data model only. It does not dictate how Offices are structured or how routing decisions are made. Offices reference Owner tags to filter OAs; they do not own the OA schema.

### Governance Status

- **Produced By:** Founder Review — Architecture Session 2026-07-05
- **Approved:** 2026-07-05
- **Registered:** 2026-07-05
- **Supersedes:** None
- **Superseded By:** None

### References

- OA-170 — Introduce Owner field to OA data model
- FOUNDER_REVIEW_CURRENT_VERSION_V1.md

