## AD-086 — AIOS Work Lifecycle

**Identifier:** AD-086
**Status:** Approved
**Approved:** 2026-07-05
**Registered:** 2026-07-05
**Initiative:** INI-001

### Decision

AIOS adopts a canonical Work Lifecycle as the single agreed process through which all work moves. Every future AIOS feature — Offices, Automations, Workers, Reports, Workspaces — must plug into this lifecycle rather than defining its own process.

### Canonical Lifecycle

```
Idea
  ↓
Discussion
  ↓
Founder Approval
  ↓
OA Created
  ↓
Owner Assigned
  ↓
Office Queue
  ↓
Workspace Opened
  ↓
AI Execution
  ↓
Review
  ↓
Founder Sign-off
  ↓
Completed
  ↓
Report Generated
  ↓
Knowledge Base Updated
  ↓
Archived
```

### Stage Definitions

| Stage | Description | AIOS System |
|-------|-------------|-------------|
| Idea | An initiative or problem is identified | Conversation, memory |
| Discussion | Idea explored with AI or Founder | Office Workspace |
| Founder Approval | Founder decides to formalise as work | OA creation |
| OA Created | Work item formally registered | OA Register |
| Owner Assigned | Office or individual takes ownership | Owner field (AD-085) |
| Office Queue | OA appears in office work queue | Office detail page |
| Workspace Opened | Active working session begins | Office Workspace |
| AI Execution | AI systems perform the work | Workers, Automation |
| Review | Output reviewed — AI and/or Founder | Office Workspace |
| Founder Sign-off | Founder approves completion | Approval action |
| Completed | OA status set to Closed | OA Register |
| Report Generated | Completion documented | Reporting system |
| Knowledge Base Updated | Learnings persisted | Second Brain (OA-185) |
| Archived | Work record preserved for reference | Archive store |

### Rationale

AIOS has accumulated: OAs, Offices, Workers, Automations, Reports, Workspaces, and an Orchestrator — each with their own implicit workflow. Without a canonical lifecycle, new features will create parallel processes that fragment the system. A single lifecycle makes AIOS coherent: the Founder always knows where any piece of work is in the same sequence.

### Implementation Note

This AD is a reference architecture only. Stages are implemented incrementally across Implementation Cycle 1. Not all stages require immediate implementation; the lifecycle provides the target state that features build toward.

### Boundary

This lifecycle governs all work that enters the OA register. Ad-hoc Founder queries and exploration that do not result in an OA are outside scope. The lifecycle does not prescribe how AI systems internally execute their work — only the external stages visible to the Founder.

