## AD-088 — AIOS Package Specification Standard

### Classification: Engineering — may be revised via standard AD process

**Initiative:** INI-001

### Summary

Defines the nine standard package types that form the internal communication
protocol of AIOS. Every AI worker consumes a structured package from AIOS and
returns a structured Report Package. AIOS is the orchestrator; no agent
communicates directly with another agent.

The nine package types: Submission, Brief, Scope Contract, Implementation,
Research, Architecture, Review, Validation, Report.

### Context

After ratifying AD-087 (Domain Model), the architectural question arose: how
do agents communicate with AIOS? Unstructured conversation was identified as
the primary gap. FR-030 (Agent Protocol and Package Specification Direction)
established the universal package principle: same structure, different purpose.
This AD formalises that principle.

### The Universal Package Principle

> Same structure. Different purpose.
> The package changes; the worker changes; the workflow does not.

Every package carries: package_id, package_type, schema_version, initiative_ref,
oa_refs, ad_refs, scope_contract_ref, payload.

### The Nine Package Types

| Package | Purpose | Producer | Consumer |
|---|---|---|---|
| Submission | External intent entering AIOS | External agents | Submission Engine |
| Brief | Scoped work proposal for Founder | Brief Engine | Founder |
| Scope Contract | Authority boundary for assigned work | AIOS (at Proceed) | All agents |
| Implementation | Input to implementation agents | AIOS | Implementation agents |
| Research | Input to research agents | AIOS | Research agents |
| Architecture | Input to architecture agents | AIOS | Architecture agents |
| Review | Input to review agents | AIOS | Review agents |
| Validation | Gate criteria at Validation Gate | AIOS | Validation agents |
| Report | Structured output from any agent | Any agent | AIOS |

### Key Rules

- Every package must carry initiative_ref. A package without Initiative
  reference is constitutionally invalid.
- AIOS is always the producer of packages sent to agents.
- Agents never produce packages for other agents — all routing via AIOS.
- No package may reference a provider name.
- All identifiers (PKG-xxx, SUB-xxx, BRF-xxx) are assigned by AIOS.
- Reports are produced by every agent on completion — silent completions
  are a governance violation.

### Full Specification

See: `SYSTEM/ARCHITECTURE/AIOS_PACKAGE_SPECIFICATION_STANDARD_CURRENT_VERSION_V1.md`

