## AD-089 — Codex Integration Standard

### Classification: Engineering — may be revised via standard AD process

**Initiative:** INI-001

### Summary

Defines the integration model for Codex as the AIOS Implementation Worker.
Specifies the Implementation Package format AIOS sends to Codex, the Scope
Contract authority boundary, the Report Package Codex returns to AIOS, and
the Validation Gate AIOS applies before closing OAs.

Codex is a role specification, not a provider binding. "Codex" names the
Implementation Worker interface. Any capable code-execution agent may fulfil
this role at runtime.

### Key Rules

- Every Implementation Package sent to Codex must carry a Scope Contract.
- Codex must validate every file path against the Scope Contract before
  making any change. Paths outside the contract are rejected and reported.
- Scope Contracts carry an expiry. Expired contracts must be rejected.
- Codex always returns a Report Package — silent completions are a governance
  violation.
- Codex never validates its own work. Validation is a separate role.
- No Implementation Package may name a specific AI provider.
- Founder authorisation (`founder_authorised: true`) is required before
  Codex may modify any governance document (SYSTEM/ directory).

### Interpretation Note — 2026-07-18 (human-mediated mode, interim)

**Gap found:** this AD states "Codex always returns a Report Package —
silent completions are a governance violation." But the real Codex work
delivered to date (OA-181–208, per `CODEX_BRIEFING.md`) was human-mediated
collaboration with no Report Packages — the formal dispatch→execution→
report cycle through `agent_runtime.py` has never completed even once
(OA-AIOS-269). Read literally, the work pattern that has actually
delivered value under this AD is a standing violation of it. Nobody
noticed because the human-mediated mode predates this AD (ratified
2026-07-07) and simply continued unexamined. Caught by Fable's
independent certification audit, 2026-07-17 (F4), not by either AI
office's own review.

**Interpretation, not a rule change:** human-mediated Codex collaboration
(no Report Package, no Scope Contract enforcement by the automated
pipeline) is hereby explicitly authorised as the **interim standard**
for Codex work, effective retroactively to 2026-07-07 through the
closure of OA-AIOS-269. This does not weaken the AD's substantive
intent — Founder authorisation for governance-document changes, scope
discipline, and validation-before-close all still apply in the
human-mediated mode, just enforced by the human relay instead of the
automated pipeline. Once OA-AIOS-269 closes (the governed runtime
completes one real dispatch→execution→report cycle), this interim
authorisation lapses and the AD's literal text — Report Packages
mandatory, no exceptions — governs without qualification.

**Why this note exists rather than a rule change:** the underlying rule
is correct and should not be diluted; the gap was that an already-real,
already-valuable work pattern was quietly out of compliance with no
one having said so. This converts an unnoticed non-compliance into a
documented, bounded, self-expiring decision.

### Addendum — 2026-07-19 (Repository Review requirement)

**Change:** Adds a "Repository Review" element to the Implementation
Package / Report Package pair, in two parts, for work where a governing
document (Master Product Spec, feature Summary, Decisions Register,
Outstanding Actions) should be checked before implementation:

- **Implementation Package side (prospective):** an instruction directing
  the worker to check the relevant governing documents before beginning
  work — the same working checklist adopted at the ZYRA level (DR-ZYRA-092,
  `ZYRA_EXECUTION_V2.md` §3.2), generalised here to the Package format.
- **Report Package side (retrospective):** a record of what was actually
  reviewed and any conflicts found, added as a new evidence field
  alongside the existing `acceptance_criteria_met` array (Part 3.3).
- **New explicit Validation Gate trigger, added to Part 4.2's three
  existing triggers:** a Repository Review present on a Report, with any
  Conflicts noted, itself sets `validation_required: true`. This is
  necessary, not implicit — the existing three triggers ("modifies
  governance documents" / OA flagged / Scope Contract carries
  `founder_authorised: true`) would only catch this incidentally, and a
  Repository Review claim that is never independently checked would be
  meaningless evidence sitting in an archived Report.

**Does not weaken the independence principle — reaffirms it.** An
instruction to perform a review (Package side) is not self-validation;
"Codex never validates its own work" (Part 4.2) still means the Report's
claimed evidence is checked by a separate Validation Worker, not trusted
on submission. The explicit new trigger exists specifically to make sure
that checking actually happens for this evidence type, rather than
leaving it to the three existing triggers to catch by chance.

**Why an addendum, not a superseding AD:** follows the precedent set by
the 2026-07-18 Interpretation Note, above — extends the Report Package
schema and Validation Gate triggers; does not change Codex's role,
authority boundaries, the Scope Contract mechanism, or the independence
principle itself.

**Origin:** Consolidated Governance Review Package, 2026-07-19, Subject
4/Item 5 — drafted jointly by Claude and ChatGPT (standing in for Codex
while offline), independently reviewed by Fable (Opus 4) across two
review cycles (first pass held pending a full read of this document's
Part 4.2 rather than CLAUDE.md's summary of it; second pass cleared on
that direct read), Founder-ratified 2026-07-19.

### Full Specification

See: `SYSTEM/ARCHITECTURE/AIOS_CODEX_INTEGRATION_MODEL_CURRENT_VERSION_V1.md`
(this addendum is recorded here only, per the same citation discipline it
enforces — not duplicated into the full specification document.)

### Governance Status

- **Produced By:** Architecture Office — 2026-07-07
- **Status:** APPROVED — 2026-07-07. Interpretation Note added 2026-07-18
  (human-mediated mode authorised as interim standard until OA-AIOS-269
  closes). Addendum added 2026-07-19 (Repository Review requirement,
  Report Package + Validation Gate) — neither changes the AD's
  substantive rules; see notes above.
