## AD-AIOS-091 — Skill Library

### Classification: Governance — requires Founder approval to amend

**Initiative:** INI-001

### Summary

Establishes the Skill Library (`SYSTEM/SKILLS/`) as the single canonical
home for reusable methodology in Black Umbrella Group. A Skill is a
governed methodology — it teaches any capable AI how to perform one
specific job to AIOS standards. Skills are provider-neutral plain markdown.

The Skill Library is the successor to Generation 1 (Agent Contract base
roles, June 2026) and to the methodology portions of Generation 2
(Operating Standards, July 2026). Identity stays in Office specs; rules
stay in Governance; methodology lives only in Skills.

### Key Rules

- Three homes, no duplication: Office specs → identity; Governance →
  rules; Skill Library → methodology. Method text elsewhere must be a
  pointer to its Skill.
- Successor rule: superseded methodology documents are archived or marked
  with supersession pointers per the records convention — never silently
  deleted. Operating Standards retain genuine rules (e.g. when a review is
  required); the how becomes the Skill.
- Skill format (fixed skeleton, soft ceiling ~150 lines): Purpose · When
  to load · Procedure · Output format · Quality bar · Context contract ·
  Governing ADs.
- Consumer rule (the Generation-1 lesson): no Skill is created without a
  consumer that exists today, named in the Skill's header.
- Skills are versioned per the CURRENT_VERSION / dated-archive convention.
- Expansion beyond the two pilot Skills is gated on pilot measurement
  (OA-AIOS-224).

### Full Specification

See: `LEAD_ARCHITECT/WORKING/SKILLS_CONTEXT_ARCHITECTURE_PROPOSAL_2026-07-12_V1.md` (approved proposal);
pilot Skills in `SYSTEM/SKILLS/`.

