## AD-AIOS-092 — Context Resolver

### Classification: Engineering — may be revised via standard AD process

**Initiative:** INI-001

### Summary

Establishes evidence resolution as a named architectural capability — the
Context Resolver — implemented by unifying the five existing engines
(context OA-181, search OA-184, second brain OA-185, repository index
OA-209, repository intelligence OA-210) behind one interface. No new
context engine is built. Completes the six-layer model: Office (identity)
→ Skills (method) → Context (evidence) → Model (reasoning) → Governance
(validation) → Records (memory).

### Key Rules

- Skills declare context contracts (evidence classes); the Resolver
  selects the items. Context selection is never a Skill — a model cannot
  select context it has not yet seen.
- Atomic vs compressible: contract-required items load whole or the
  dispatch fails loudly; history/reports/memory compress best-effort
  within remaining budget. No silent drop of an atomic item, ever.
- Resolution order: contract resolution → dependency expansion (OA-210)
  → relevance fill to budget.
- Stages 1–2 are deterministic and local (AD-083). AI-assisted triage is
  permitted only within relevance fill, only in Phase 2/3, and only with
  feedback-loop evidence justifying it.
- Feedback loop: rejected/reworked outputs are correlated with their
  dispatch's resolver drop log (mirrors the provider-routing quality loop).
- The Resolver operates on existing repository objects only; its sole
  owned artifact is the evidence-class definition
  (`SYSTEM/SKILLS/CONTEXT_EVIDENCE_CLASSES_CURRENT_VERSION_V1.md`).

### Full Specification

See: `CONTEXT_INTELLIGENCE_DISCOVERY_RESEARCH_2026-07-12_V1.md` (evidence
base) and the approved proposal (as AD-AIOS-091).

### Governance Status

- **Produced By:** Fable (independent research + proposal), on Research
  Office (ChatGPT) recommendation — 2026-07-12
