## AD-AIOS-093 — Unified Agent Architecture: Dispatch View and Lifecycle View

### Classification: Governance — requires Founder approval to amend

**Initiative:** INI-001

### Summary

Ratifies one architecture model for how work moves through AIOS's Office/
Skill/Context/Model/Governance/Records system, resolving a duplication
risk Fable's independent audit flagged
(`AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_INDEPENDENT_AUDIT_2026-07-17_V1.md` §5): a five-layer
"dispatch" model (discussed 2026-07-17 between Founder Office and Research
Office) and the six-layer "lifecycle" model already established under
AD-AIOS-091/092 were two separately-described views of the same system,
with no single document stating how they relate — the same kind of
unresolved duplication that let the Roadmap V12 Phase 3/Phase 4 offices
ambiguity go unnoticed until an independent audit found it. This AD states,
once, which view is canonical for what, incorporates the deterministic-
lane fork Fable's audit required, and writes down the precise atomicity
definition Skills must follow.

### Key Rules

1. **One system, two views — not two competing models.** The six-layer
   Lifecycle View (Office → Skills → Context → Model → Governance →
   Records, established under AD-AIOS-091/092) is canonical for the full
   arc of one unit of work, from identity through to memory. The Dispatch
   View (below) is the front portion of that same lifecycle — the
   WHO/WHEN/WHAT decisions that happen before Context resolution and
   Model execution — not a separate architecture.

2. **Dispatch View, ratified:**
   - **WHO** — Office. Identity and accountability for the work. Per
     Founder Review Area 4: today this is an accountability claim, not
     yet a behaviour claim — Offices currently run identical pipeline
     code with different prompts. Real, but not to be read as claiming
     distinct office behaviour that doesn't exist yet.
   - **WHEN — the fork.** Every trigger resolves to exactly one of two
     lanes:
     - *Deterministic lane (default, AD-083):* a direct engine call — no
       Skill, no Context Resolver, no Model. Confirmed live: all 7 of
       today's automations run this lane exclusively. This is correct,
       not a shortfall — AD-083 exists specifically to keep local,
       mechanical work out of the AI path.
     - *AI lane:* Skill Selector → Context Resolver → Model (Runtime).
       Reserved for work that genuinely needs reasoning over evidence.
     WHEN sources are not limited to Automations — the Founder's manual
     briefs are today's dominant trigger and belong on this layer too.
   - **WHAT** — Skill Selector, when the AI lane is taken. Recommends
     which Skill(s) apply; never dispatches or executes
     (`SKILL_SELECTOR_CURRENT_VERSION_V1.md` §1).
   - Evidence and reasoning (Context, Model) are the Lifecycle View's own
     layers 3–4 — the Dispatch View hands off to them, it does not
     duplicate them.

3. **Atomicity, precisely defined.** A Skill may contain internal
   sequential steps belonging to ONE methodology —
   `evidence-first-investigation`'s four internal stages are correctly
   one Skill, not four. What a Skill must never do is invoke or compose
   other Skills; composition is the Selector/Resolver's job alone, never
   a Skill's. A Skill that orchestrates other Skills is architecturally a
   second orchestrator and is prohibited regardless of size. Line-count
   ("~150 lines") is a heuristic proxy for this rule, not the rule itself
   — a multi-step single-methodology Skill may legitimately exceed it; a
   short Skill that composes others violates the rule regardless of
   length.

4. **No silent AI-ification of the deterministic lane.** An automation or
   engine call may not be "upgraded" to route through the Skill Selector
   or Context Resolver without a new AD or OA explicitly authorising it.
   This rule exists because the fork (rule 2) is easy to blur by degrees
   — one call moved to the AI lane "just this once" — and AD-083's
   local-first default depends on the boundary staying explicit, not
   eroding by accretion.

5. **Governance and Records remain the Lifecycle View's own territory**,
   unaffected by this AD: validation (Governed Review, AD-090's
   Investigation Pipeline) and memory (execution records, timeline,
   feedback logs per AD-AIOS-092 §12) apply identically regardless of
   which Dispatch lane produced the work.

### Full Specification

Dispatch View mechanics are specified in
`SKILL_SELECTOR_CURRENT_VERSION_V1.md` and
`CONTEXT_RESOLVER_CURRENT_VERSION_V1.md`. Lifecycle View mechanics are
specified in AD-AIOS-091 (Skill Library) and AD-AIOS-092 (Context
Resolver). This AD does not restate either — it states how they relate
and closes the three gaps Fable's audit found in the informally-discussed
five-layer model.

### Governance Status

- **Produced By:** Founder Office (Claude), ratifying a joint Founder
  Office / Research Office (ChatGPT) discussion of 2026-07-17, with three
