## AD-AIOS-097 — AI Team Restructure 2: Codex as Lead Architect; Fable and Claude as Executors; Fable as Documentation Owner

### Classification: Governance — requires Founder approval to amend

**Initiative:** INI-003 (Black Umbrella Group Operations)

### Summary

Re-binds the providers behind the permanent role interfaces (FR-030/FR-031,
unchanged) and inverts AD-AIOS-094's execution structure: Codex becomes Lead
Architect and does not implement; Fable and Claude become the Executors; Fable
becomes the single documentation owner across BLACK UMBRELLA GROUP and ZYRA.
Source: Founder instruction of 2026-08-17 (relayed in session — per
AI_TEAM_WORKING_PROTOCOL §1.2, the Founder's direct instruction is the
approval), following Fable's evidence review of the same day
(REPORTS/CURRENT/FABLE_GOVERNANCE_REVIEW_2026-08-17_V1.md), accepted by Codex
as Lead Architect.

### Key Rules

1. Provider re-bindings (Layer 3; role interfaces permanent):

| Role interface (permanent) | Prior provider (AD-AIOS-094) | New provider |
|---|---|---|
| Architecture Agent / Lead Architect | Claude Opus | **Codex** |
| Implementation Agent / Executors | Claude Opus (primary lead) | **Fable** (product/UX) and **Claude** (engineering/database) — one named executor per brief |
| UX / Product Experience Agent | Fable | Fable (unchanged) |
| Documentation Owner (NEW single-owner assignment) | held by the Lead Architect seat | **Fable** |
| Research / Strategy Agent | ChatGPT | ChatGPT — binding not changed by this AD; default-loop membership is an open Founder decision (OA-AIOS-299, D1) |
| Orchestrator | AIOS engine | AIOS engine (unchanged) |
| Founder | Shakeel | Shakeel (unchanged) |

2. Codex — Lead Architect: defines architecture, scope, quality gates and
   evidence requirements; authors task briefs, each naming exactly one
   executor; reviews returned evidence against the gates; recommends to the
   Founder. Codex does not edit files, does not run git, does not author or
   run database migrations, does not implement, and does not approve its own
   proposals.
3. Fable and Claude — Executors: implement approved briefs and return
   evidence. Executors do not change scope or architecture unilaterally, do
   not run git, and do not approve work — including their own. Where
   implementation uncovers evidence against an approved design, the executor
   stops and raises it (existing law, ZYRA CLAUDE.md §2).
4. Documentation single-owner: Fable holds all documentation edits — governed
   documents and registers — across BLACK UMBRELLA GROUP and ZYRA. Executing
   agents draft register-entry text for their own work; Fable files it.
5. The Founder remains the only approval authority. Agreement between AIs is
   never approval (AI_TEAM_WORKING_PROTOCOL §1.1 — unchanged). The Founder's
   direct instruction is the approval (§1.2 — unchanged).
6. Default workflow: Founder → Codex (brief) → named Executor → Codex
   (evidence review) → Founder approval.
7. AD-AIOS-094 rules 2, 6 and 7 and its provider-binding table are
   superseded. AD-AIOS-094 rule 8 (Founder-dispatched independent review for
   security, payments, architecture, large migrations, major governance)
   remains in force unchanged.
8. The provider-neutral Implementation Worker interface (AD-089) is
   unaffected as an interface. The provider instance named Codex no longer
   fulfils it; the executor seats do. A status note to this effect is
   recorded in AIOS_CODEX_INTEGRATION_MODEL_CURRENT_VERSION_V1.md. The
   dormant automated pipeline (OA-AIOS-269) is not redesigned by this AD.

### Open Founder Decisions

Tracked as OA-AIOS-299: D1 — ChatGPT's seat (default loop vs on-dispatch);
D2 — default verification of executor work beyond the Lead Architect's
evidence review; D4 — when to re-enable overnight schedules and at what
budget (the 2026-08-01 Founder pause stands until then).

