## AD-AIOS-098 — Offices and Agents Rationalisation: Three Agent Classes, One Register of Record

### Classification: Governance — requires Founder approval to amend

**Initiative:** INI-001 (AIOS Platform Operations)

### Summary

Ratifies the full review of AIOS's Offices and agents against the AD-AIOS-097
team, and establishes `AIOS_OFFICES_AND_AGENTS_CURRENT_VERSION_V1.md`
(SYSTEM/ARCHITECTURE/) as the single register of record for who does work in
AIOS — offices, agents, seats, contracts, Claude/Codex/Fable assignment,
collaboration lanes, task routing and escalation — with a machine copy at
`AIOS/WORKSPACE_DATA/org_structure.json` rendered by the Workspace Team page.
Source: Founder brief "AIOS Offices, Agents & Claude/Codex Assignment Review",
2026-08-18 (direct instruction — the approval, per AI_TEAM_WORKING_PROTOCOL
§1.2).

### Key Rules

1. Three agent classes, exhaustively: **Seats** (AD-AIOS-097 team — decide
   and build, human-relayed), **Offices** (four API reasoning agents — think
   on demand, can change nothing), **System agents** (eleven deterministic
   automations under the Heartbeat — no AI, no spend).
2. Office verdicts: Founder / Development / Research / Security — KEEP with
   bindings modified to AD-AIOS-097 (pre-097 "Primary/Secondary AI" charter
   bindings retired); Architecture Office — REMOVED, confirming its
   2026-07-15 absorption (OA-AIOS-258); Marketing/Legal/Accounting offices —
   CREATE REFUSED for now (no recurring workload; the Workspace spaces carry
   visibility, Research Office carries the analysis).
3. Agent verdicts: Generation-1 contracts (both trees) — REMOVED as live
   agents, historical record only (confirms the 2026-07-12 supersession under
   AD-AIOS-091; this AD is the ZYRA tree's missing supersession notice). The
   six Generation-1 runtime workers of 2026-07-05 (incl. the Architecture
   Review worker failing against the absorbed office since 27 Jul, and the
   Morning Briefing / Nightly Summary / Backup / Usage Digest duplicates) —
   REMOVED from the worker registry/schedule/state, run history retained,
   stranded 5-Jul queue item cleared. The eleven automation workers — KEEP
   as the single scheduling generation.
4. Assignment: architecture, planning, gates, audits, contradiction
   detection, evidence review → Codex. Code, debugging, testing, repository
   and database inspection, technical verification → Claude. UI/product
   implementation, UX, documentation and register filing → Fable. Research →
   Research Office; ChatGPT on Founder dispatch (D1 open). Security: Codex
   designs, Claude changes, deterministic scans stay local.
5. Three lanes, one spine: the brief lane (changes anything; ZYRA-only
   lane), the Office lane (Founder-pressed, budgeted, changes nothing), the
   deterministic lane (Heartbeat). The registers are the spine; one named
   executor per brief; bounded single review against pre-stated gates;
   Founder-dispatched independent review for high-risk classes (AD-AIOS-094
   rule 8, unchanged).
6. Documentation-vs-implementation conflicts found and resolved: stale
   charter bindings (superseded by the register of record); the orphaned
   Architecture worker (removed); duplicate worker generations (collapsed);
   the ZYRA Generation-1 contracts lacking a supersession note (this AD);
   `workspace.py`'s legacy OA parser blind to Enterprise-format ids
   (already raised in OA-AIOS-300 — for the Lead Architect to brief).

### Governance Status

