AD-AIOS-104
Title:       No Undocumented Intelligence — BUILD -> DOCUMENT ->
             TRACE -> HANDOVER is a company-wide completion rule
Date:        2026-08-23
Status:      APPROVED — direct Founder instruction
Owner:       Founder (Shakeel)
Classification: Governance / Engineering Memory — applies to every
                Black Umbrella Group project and AI-assisted build

Decision:
  1. Meaningful work follows BUILD -> DOCUMENT -> TRACE -> HANDOVER.
     A feature or system may not exist only in chat, a temporary session,
     a builder's memory or undocumented code.
  2. The implementer creates/updates the governed as-built handover with
     what/why, exact files and architecture, data flow and entry points,
     developer controls/readers, mock versus production, migrations,
     named tests/measurements, limitations/OAs and next steps.
  3. Fable, as Documentation Owner, checks the handover against actual code
     and evidence; reconciles product specification, build contract and
     as-built reality; files registers; removes CURRENT_VERSION ambiguity;
     and regenerates indexes.
  4. Product specification, build contract and as-built handover own three
     different questions. Differences are named and receive an OA or written
     refusal; no hidden assumptions.
  5. CODE_COMPLETE, HANDOVER_COMPLETE, independent review and Founder
     approval are distinct states and must never be reported as each other.
  6. The governed/manual gate is live now. Automated engine enforcement is
     not yet implemented and remains OA-AIOS-363.

Governing implementation:
  IMPLEMENTATION_HANDOVER_STANDARD_CURRENT_VERSION_V1;
  GOVERNANCE V11 Principle 15; AI_TEAM_WORKING_PROTOCOL V4 §2;
  AIOS_LEAD_ARCHITECT_BRIEFING V3; AIOS_OFFICES_AND_AGENTS V3;
  AIOS_EXECUTION_ENGINE V3 AC-20.

Concurrency record:
  Two same-minute standard drafts were detected. The correctly placed,
  more complete MASTER_STANDARDS document is canonical; the second is
  archived as AIOS_HANDOVER_STANDARD_2026-08-23_V1 with explicit
  supersession. No identifier collision occurred because live NEXT values
  were re-read before append.

Evidence/trace: OA-AIOS-363; OA-ZYRA-251/252; ZYRA Guardian Network as-built
                handover (reference implementation).

